<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 36,933 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 36,933 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 36,933 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 104,064 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			18,843	    19,377</p>
<p>    Import cargo			18,090	    84,687</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and four berthed.</p>
<p>In the next 24 hours, four ship was expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	     Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		68,000	 Johar		   4/4</p>
<p>Jet oil		  25,000	 Ras Al Zour	   5/4</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Warbah		  5/4</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Ying Song Hu	  1/4</p>
<p>Motor gasoline	 25,000	 Sen Sabastian	 2/4</p>
<p>Gas oil		  48,000	 Obo Victory	   due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
